{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:18.200.070","page_type":"section"},"citation":"18.200.070","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.200.070","content_hash":"e6c1bb7a3472c47d3d8c004965eeeaa7e16a48db470eb2b0b38052bbe69f26cd","heading":"Parking.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.200.070:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.200.070","text":"(a) No off-street parking requirements for the D-1, D-3 use districts.\n(b) Minimum off-street parking requirements for the D-2 use districts shall be consistent with the following:\n(1) Residential dwellings: one space per dwelling unit.\n(2) Private clubs, drinking establishments, and restaurants: one space per four occupants permitted.\n(3) Retail and office uses: one space per 500 square feet of usable retail or office floor area.\n(4) All other uses not specified shall be consistent with Chapter 18.240 TMC.\n(c) A maximum number of off-street parking spaces for a particular use may be required by the Planning Director to conserve open space, prevent unnecessary demolition of buildings and damage to the historic integrity of a district, or to remain consistent with adopted development performance standards. (Ord. 17661 § 7, 8-20-01. Code 1995 § 48-24b.05.)\nCross References: Planning and Development Department, TMC 2.20.080 .","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"697ff8a2-1476-52c5-a81f-fd8b5c344901"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.200.070","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.200.070","content_hash":"790dd5670dd18aac0ed92f8de035ea838b1aa3a23b04a2ad9c7655619c1746a8","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.200.070:section","sc